[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "London System"]
[Variation "Queen's Pawn Game: Accelerated London System"]
[ECO "D00"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "b2-pressure,transposition"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "2.Bf4"]
[Start "orthodox 1...d5"]

2. Bf4 { The bishop comes out before e3 is played, so it is never shut in behind its own pawns. } 2... c5 { White's bishop is out before the knight, so ...c5 hits d4 at once while e3 is still unplayed. } 3. e3 ( 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. e3 Nf6 ) ( 3. c3 Nc6 4. e3 ) ( 3. dxc5 Nf6 { Black develops first and takes the pawn back later. } 4. e3 e6 ) 3... Nc6 { A second attacker on d4. } 4. c3 Qb6 { Hits the loose b2 pawn and d4 together. } 5. Qb3 ( 5. Qc2 Nf6 6. Nf3 Nh5 ) 5... c4 { Attacks the queen and keeps the centre closed. } 6. Qxb6 axb6 7. Nd2 Nf6 { Develops with no weaknesses. After Ngf3 this is the main line again. } 8. Ngf3 *
